<p class="lt-chem-21770"><strong class="emphasis bold">A.</strong> Of the species listed, xenon (Xe), ethane (C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>6</sub>), and trimethylamine [(CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>N] do not contain a hydrogen atom attached to O, N, or F; hence they cannot act as hydrogen bond donors.</p>

